            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/A> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.11.2/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/341> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/341>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Qualité de l'enquête relative à l'exercice 2009"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2011-01-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/Fiche_qualite_SRCV2009.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.10>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.10>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.10/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.10/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.2.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.2.3>
                    "2016-04-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/uniteEnquetee/H> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.10.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/345> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/344> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/343> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The survey is conducted face-to-face from May to June using computer assisted personal inter-aided method. The data is collected annually in the form of a panel survey.</p>\n<p>The principle consists in surveying the same sample of households and individuals in nine consecutive years in France (Most of the countries have a rotational design based on four rotational groups as recommended by Eurostat).</p>\n<p>Unlike other surveys of households, a household questionnaire is completed and an individual questionnaire is completed for each person aged 16 years or over in the household.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.8>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.8>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/modeCollecte/F> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/geo/territoireFrancais/franceMetropolitaine> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Chaque ann&eacute;e, un module dit &laquo;primaire&raquo; permet d'aborder les th&egrave;mes suivants :</p>\n<p>- caract&eacute;ristiques sociod&eacute;mographiques des personnes appartenant aux m&eacute;nages dans lesquels ils vivent ;</p>\n<p>- d&eacute;tail des revenus per&ccedil;us l'ann&eacute;e civile pr&eacute;c&eacute;dant la collecte ;</p>\n<p>- situation financi&egrave;re des m&eacute;nages : &eacute;pargne, endettement&hellip; ;</p>\n<p>- conditions de vie : indicateurs de privation, logement et &eacute;quipement, environnement et sant&eacute;.</p>\n<p>Un module secondaire dit &laquo;ad hoc&raquo; est introduit chaque ann&eacute;e depuis 2005. Il permet d'approfondir certains th&egrave;mes comme l'&eacute;quipement et les commodit&eacute;s du logement, le surendettement et l'exclusion, les privations mat&eacute;rielles, etc...</p>\n<p>Les donn&eacute;es issues de ces modules compl&eacute;mentaires figurent dans le rapport annuel de printemps destin&eacute; au Conseil europ&eacute;en.</p>\n<p>Par ailleurs, la France a introduit &agrave; partir de 2008 un questionnement suppl&eacute;mentaire d'indicateurs sociaux dont les th&egrave;mes &eacute;taient trait&eacute;s par les anciennes enqu&ecirc;tes permanentes des conditions de vie (EPCV).</p>\n<p>Trois modules ont &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;finis, chacun sera pos&eacute; tous les 3 ans :</p>\n<p>- le premier module porte sur la sant&eacute;, la vie associative, les relations professionnelles et la participation sociale ;</p>\n<p>- le deuxi&egrave;me sur les sports et les loisirs ;</p>\n<p>- le troisi&egrave;me sur la mobilit&eacute; sociale et les contacts avec les proches.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/345>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "La méthodologie de l'enquête Statistiques sur les Ressources et les Conditions de Vie / SRCV"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2015-12-21"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/MET_SRCV_2016.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.1.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.10.6>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.10.6>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.10.6/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.4/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Each year, the target primary areas cover the following themes:</p>\n<p>- socio-demographic characteristics of households members;</p>\n<p>- components of annual income: income from employment, property income, government transfers received, current transfers from&nbsp;other households etc ;</p>\n<p>- labour information;</p>\n<p>- financial situation of households: savings, debt etc;</p>\n<p>- living conditions: indicators of material deprivation, housing and equipment, environment and health.</p>\n<p>A so-called \"ad hoc\" secondary module has been added each year since 2005. It goes in greater depth into certain topics, such as the equipment and commodities of the dwelling, over-indebtedness, material deprivation, etc.</p>\n<p>The data from these complementary modules are included in the annual spring report to the European Council.</p>\n<p>In addition to this, since 2008, France introduced supplementary questions on social indicators : some of them were present in the former survey on living conditions (EPCV).</p>\n<p>Three sets of supplementary questions have been defined, each being applied every three years:</p>\n<p>- the first one is on health, associative activities, professional relationships and social participation;</p>\n<p>- the second on sports and recreation;</p>\n<p>- he third on social mobility and contacts with close personal relations.</p>\n<p>Since 2008, a statistical matching is made with the tax sources for the year, in particular with. the tax returns for year N. The amounts of social benefits actually received by the households over the reference year N are collected directly from the three main Benefit funds in France: the national family allowances fund (CNAF), the national old-age insurance fund (CNAV) and the central agricultural social insurance fund (CCMSA).</p>\n<p>A self-administered questionnaire on well-being has been introduced since 2010 in the french part of the EU-SILC. Every year, a sub-sample (one-ninths) is concerned.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.1.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/344>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Le rapport intermédiaire sur la qualité des données françaises E.U.-S.I.L.C 2009"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2011-07-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/Rapport_qualite_SILC_2009_intermediaire.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.10/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Environ 12 000 ménages interrogés chaque année, dont 10 000 ménages environ ont déjà été interrogés l'année précédente."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "About 12,000 households surveyed each year. At the first year, nine panels of individuals are drawn. Each year, one panel is dropped out and a new one is substituted for. It is therefore a rotating sample renewed by one-ninths."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/343>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Pondération dans les échantillons rotatifs : le cas de l'enquête SILC en France"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2007-12-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/ArticleSILC_Ardilly_Lavallee_fr.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Rapport qualité : Statistiques sur les ressources et conditions de vie 2009"@fr , "Quality report: Statistics on income and living conditions 2009"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/operations/operation/s1075> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.4>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.4/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.3.4/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.3/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>L'enqu&ecirc;te est r&eacute;alis&eacute;e en face &agrave; face de mai &agrave; juin par un mode de collecte assist&eacute; par informatique (Capi). Les donn&eacute;es sont collect&eacute;es annuellement sous la forme d'une enqu&ecirc;te en panel.</p>\n<p>Le principe consiste &agrave; interroger le m&ecirc;me &eacute;chantillon de m&eacute;nages et individus neuf ann&eacute;es de suite.</p>\n<p>Ainsi, chaque ann&eacute;e, un nouvel &eacute;chantillon de 3 000 fiches adresses vient alimenter le panel ; un &eacute;chantillon de m&eacute;nages dit \"sortant\" quitte alors le panel. Il s'agit donc d'un &eacute;chantillon rotatif renouvel&eacute; par neuvi&egrave;me.</p>\n<p>L'enqu&ecirc;te se pr&eacute;sente sous la forme d'un questionnaire m&eacute;nage et de questionnaires individuels. Chaque personne &acirc;g&eacute;e de 16 ans ou plus appartenant au m&eacute;nage interrog&eacute; se voit proposer un questionnaire individuel.&nbsp;</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.3>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.3/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1642/S.18.3/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1642> .
}

<http://rdf.insee.fr/graphes/qualite/rapport/1763> {
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.10.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The building (BT) indices are cost indices for different construction activity, apprehended from 6 positions in a cost accounting approach : \"labour costs\" once called \"salaries and expenses\", \"materials\" , \"material\", \"energy\", \"transport\", \"miscellaneous expenses\", similar to the productivity economists' approach called \"KLEMS\" (K = capital for \"equipment\", L = &ldquo;Labour&rdquo; ,\" E =&nbsp;\"energy\", M = \"materials\", S = &ldquo;Services&rdquo; for miscellaneous expenses).<br />The structure and weights of the building (BT) indices have been reviewed on the occasion of the change in base and reference 2010.<br />BT indices are chained Laspeyres indices at all levels (of elementary indices from public statistics to cost items, from cost items to BT indices).</p>\n<p>(See also methodological note)</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/738> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/597> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/702> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/739> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/740> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.19>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.19>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.19/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.19/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.18.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/M> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.2.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.2.3>
                    "2017-03-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The table in the field \"Documentation\" provides the weights of the different building indices by KLEMST cost item.</p>\n<p>It was not possible to conduct a direct approach for the costs index \"all trades\" BT01 and BT50, so their weights were therefore estimated as a weighted average of the specialized indices' weights. The weights used for this purpose, presented in the first&nbsp;two columns of the table above are from the source ESANE managed by INSEE, by sub-classes of activity, using information from ESA built on the relative share of work in the sector of new buildings (for BT01) and for existing buildings (for the BT50).<br />Specialized index weighting is realised according to subclass of activity and consistency with corresponding BT indices available above (but there is no source on the relative weight of BT indices within a subclass of activity). However, the renovation projects are more labour-intensive and less materials intensive, and specialized indices are estimated from the new buildings indices,&nbsp;with a transfer of 15 points between the materials and the labour cost items.</p>\n<p>The BT index does not give rise to a new survey, but uses existing public statistics, including those from the survey Prices in&nbsp;the industry and services (OPISE) to form the elementary indices.<br />Conceptually, the observation unit on its costs is a branch or sub-branch of activity of French construction companies or construction related companies.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Quality report: Building Index base 2010"@en , "Rapport qualité : Index bâtiment base 2010"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/produits/indicateur/p1623> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Coût, construction"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/I.18.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/uniteEnquetee/E> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/597>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Building indices, Civil engineering indices and various indices for construction"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "en" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2017-05-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/MET_INDEX_BAT_BT_BASE_2010_GB.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/739>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Poste materiel des index BT et TP base 2010"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/MET_POSTE_MATERIEL_INDEX_BT_TP_2010.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.3.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/geo/pays/france> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/M> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/738>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Correspondance entre les nouveaux et les anciens index BT"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/MET_CORRESP_ENTRE_NOUV_ANC_INDEX_BT.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.19/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The BT indices are released during the third month following the month under review, on the site of the Macro-economic database&nbsp;(BDM) in the theme \"Prices and price indices\" under \"Construction producer price and costs indices \" / \"Indices of production costs in construction (contract escalation).\"<br />It is also published in the Official Journal.&nbsp;</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.3.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Le tableau de la rubrique &laquo;&nbsp;Documentation &raquo; fournit les pond&eacute;rations des diff&eacute;rents index b&acirc;timent par poste KLEMST.</p>\n<p>Les index BT ne donnent pas lieu &agrave; une enqu&ecirc;te nouvelle, mais utilisent les statistiques publiques existantes, notamment le dispositif OPISE, pour constituer les indices &eacute;l&eacute;mentaires.<br />Conceptuellement, l'unit&eacute; observ&eacute;e sur ses co&ucirc;ts est une branche ou sous-branche d'activit&eacute; des entreprises fran&ccedil;aises de construction.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.19/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Les index BT sont diffus&eacute;s au cours du troisi&egrave;me mois suivant le mois sous revue, sur le site de la BDM, dans le th&egrave;me &laquo;&nbsp;Prix et indices de prix&nbsp;&raquo;, rubrique &laquo;&nbsp;Indices des prix de production et de co&ucirc;ts dans la construction&nbsp;&raquo;, sous-rubrique &laquo;&nbsp;Indices des co&ucirc;ts de production dans la construction (indexation de contrats)&nbsp;&raquo;.<br />Ils sont aussi publi&eacute;s au Journal Officiel.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.1.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1763> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1763/S.10.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Les index b&acirc;timent (BT) sont des indices de co&ucirc;ts des diff&eacute;rentes activit&eacute;s du secteur de la construction, appr&eacute;hend&eacute;s &agrave; partir&nbsp;de 6 postes dans une d&eacute;marche de comptabilit&eacute; analytique : &laquo;&nbsp;co&ucirc;t du travail&nbsp;&raquo; jadis appel&eacute; &laquo;&nbsp;salaires et charges&nbsp;&raquo;, &laquo;&nbsp;mat&eacute;riaux&nbsp;&raquo;, &laquo;&nbsp;mat&eacute;riel&nbsp;&raquo;, &laquo;&nbsp;&eacute;nergie&nbsp;&raquo;, &laquo;&nbsp;transport&nbsp;&raquo;, &laquo;&nbsp;frais divers&nbsp;&raquo;, analogue &agrave; l'approche &laquo;&nbsp;KLEMS&nbsp;&raquo; des &eacute;conomistes de la productivit&eacute; (K = capital pour &laquo;&nbsp;mat&eacute;riel&nbsp;&raquo;, L = labour pour &laquo;&nbsp;travail&nbsp;&raquo;, E = energy pour &laquo;&nbsp;&eacute;nergie&nbsp;&raquo;, M = materials pour &laquo;&nbsp;mat&eacute;riaux&nbsp;&raquo;, S = services pour &laquo;&nbsp;frais divers&nbsp;&raquo;).<br />La structure et les pond&eacute;rations des index BT ont &eacute;t&eacute; revues, &agrave; l'occasion de la base et r&eacute;f&eacute;rence 2010.<br />Les index BT sont des indices de Laspeyres cha&icirc;n&eacute;s &agrave; tous les niveaux (d'indices &eacute;l&eacute;mentaires issus de la statistique publique &agrave; postes, de postes &agrave; index.</p>\n<p>(Voir aussi la note m&eacute;thodologique)</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/738> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/737> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/739> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/566> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/740> .
    
