            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.4>
                    "dimensionless value other than PC, PCPA and POINTS"@en , "valeur sans dimension autre que PC, PCPA et POINTS"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1777> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.3.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/territoire/franceHorsMayotte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1777> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.10.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>&Agrave; compter de 2016 le calcul des indices de chiffre d'affaires est r&eacute;alis&eacute; &agrave; partir de l'exhaustivit&eacute; des d&eacute;clarations mensuelles de la source fiscale. Cette nouvelle m&eacute;thodologie de calcul des indices a &eacute;t&eacute; mise en &oelig;uvre pour mieux prendre en compte la d&eacute;mographie des entreprises et ainsi refl&eacute;ter plus pr&eacute;cis&eacute;ment la r&eacute;alit&eacute; &eacute;conomique. En effet les indices de chiffre d'affaires d'une ann&eacute;e N pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment calcul&eacute;s ne prenaient pas en compte les cr&eacute;ations d'entreprises, cessations, entr&eacute;es et sorties de champ et changement de secteur survenues au cours de l'ann&eacute;e N, l'&eacute;chantillon &eacute;tant tir&eacute; au 31/12 de l'ann&eacute;e N-1. Dans le cadre d'un projet de r&eacute;novation des indices de chiffres d'affaires, des solutions ont &eacute;t&eacute; mises en &oelig;uvre pour corriger ce biais et produire des indices de chiffre d'affaires de meilleure qualit&eacute;. Il s'agit, d'une part, de s'affranchir des &eacute;chantillons annuels en exploitant la totalit&eacute; des d&eacute;clarations mensuelles de TVA, les progr&egrave;s de l'informatique permettant aujourd'hui de traiter de tr&egrave;s&nbsp;gros volumes de donn&eacute;es ; d'autre part de s'appuyer sur le r&eacute;pertoire statistique Sirus &agrave; la place du r&eacute;pertoire administratif Sirene, de mani&egrave;re &agrave; b&eacute;n&eacute;ficier d'une mise &agrave; disposition beaucoup plus rapide et automatis&eacute;e des &eacute;v&eacute;nements d&eacute;mographiques les plus r&eacute;cents ayant affect&eacute; les entreprises.<br />Les indices de chiffre d'affaires dans l'industrie et la construction sont des indices mensuels en valeur (en euros courants hors taxe). Ces indices sont calcul&eacute;s en r&eacute;f&eacute;rence 100 en 2010 (les indices ont pour moyenne 100 en 2010). Ils sont calcul&eacute;s comme des indices de Laspeyres, &agrave; pond&eacute;rations constantes dans le temps des indices les plus fins, et font l'objet d'un rebasement tous les 5 ans.<br />Les indices de chiffre d'affaires dans l'industrie et la construction sont corrig&eacute;s des variations saisonni&egrave;res (CVS) et des effets de calendrier (correction des jours ouvrables &ndash; CJO).</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/116> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/83> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/115> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/79> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/114> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.10.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>From 2016 the calculation of the turnover indices is realised from the exhaustivity of the monthly declarations of the fiscal source. This new methodology of calculation of the indices was implemented to take better into account the demography of companies and so it shows more precisely the economic reality. Indeed the indices of turnover of one year N previously calculated did not take into account new business start-ups, terminations, entrances into the statistic sphere, exits of the statistic sphere, and changes of sector which happened during the year N, the sample being done the 31/12 of the year N-1. Within the framework of a&nbsp;project for a renovation of the turnovers indices, solutions were implemented to correct this bias and to produce turnover indices with better quality. On one hand, annual samples will not be used anymore and all of the monthly declarations of VAT will be&nbsp;exploited, the progress of the computing allowing to handle very big volumes of data nowadays; on the other hand, the statistical directory Sirus will be used instead of the administrative directory Siren, so as to benefit from a provision much faster and&nbsp;automated of the most recent demographic events companies have been affected.<br />Turnover indices in industry and construction are monthly indices of value in current euros excluding VAT. These indices are calculated in relation to a reference of 100 in 2010 (the indices had a mean of 100 in 2010).They are calculated as Laspeyres indices, with constant weightings over time of the most discriminating indices, and are rebased every five years.<br />Turnover indices in industry and construction are adjusted for seasonal variations (SDA) and for calendar effects (adjustment for working days &ndash; WDA).</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/627> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/626> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/616> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/I.18.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/uniteEnquetee/E> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1777> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.1.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1777> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.18.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Turnover indices are calculated based on tax data, i.e. the CA3 declaration, the form which businesses must fill in each month or each quarter for the payment of VAT.<br />They include the full turnover of declaring businesses, all activities included, classified according to the business's principal activity.<br />For exports outside the European Union and products supplied within the Community, the Turnover Indices are established according to the amount of turnover declared by enterprises. They are used to monitor the turnover, given in euros, with foreign countries.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.18.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.18.1/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1777/S.18.1/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1777> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/83>
