<http://rdf.insee.fr/graphes/qualite/rapport/1689> {
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>People of any age living in ordinary households in metropolitan France and overseas departments.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.20/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'enquête Handicap-santé - Volet Aidants informels / HSASite de la Drees<br /><a href=' http://www.drees.sante.gouv.fr/ '> http://www.drees.sante.gouv.fr/ </a> <br /><br />L'enquête Handicap-santé - Volet Ménages ordinaires / HSMSite de la Drees<br /><a href=' http://www.drees.sante.gouv.fr/ '> http://www.drees.sante.gouv.fr/ </a> <br /><br />"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.19>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.19>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.19/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.19/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.10.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/262> , <http://bauhaus/documents/document/258> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The sample was taken from the database of respondents to the filter survey Everyday Life and Health (VQS), administered in 2007 to approximately 140,000 households (size of sample includes local extensions)."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.10/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'échantillon est tiré dans la base des répondants à l'enquête de filtrage Vie Quotidienne et Santé (VQS), effectuée en 2007 auprès d'environ 140 000 ménages (taille de l'échantillon y compris les extensions locales)."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.19/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The Research, Studies, Appraisal and Statistics department (DREES) added a survey of informal carers (HAS) to this Health and Disability Survey - Ordinary Households Section 2008 (HSM).<br /><br />This HSA survey characterises the non-professional carers (family,&nbsp;friends, neighbours, etc.) of people that in the HSM survey declared their difficulties in accomplishing certain acts of daily life due to a disability, a health problem or their age.<br /><br />The survey responds to the issues raised in the recent public debate&nbsp;(Family Conference in 2006) concerning the organisation of an entitlement to respite for family carers. Approximately 5,000 people aged 16 and over were interviewed.<br /><br />The socio-demographic characteristics of the carers in the family circle were covered;&nbsp;the consequences of helping on the carers' family and professional lives, their health, leisure time, relationships with professional carers (from the health and social sectors) and their complementarity.<br /><br />In addition, the Institution section of the Health and Disability Survey (HSI) was administered in 2009.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Rapport qualité : Enquête Handicap-Santé - volet ménages 2008"@fr , "Quality report: Health and disability survey - households section 2008"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/operations/operation/s1387> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.2.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.2.3>
                    "2016-03-25"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.19/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>La Direction de la recherche, des &eacute;tudes, de l'&eacute;valuation et des statistiques (Drees) adosse &agrave; cette enqu&ecirc;te Handicap-sant&eacute; - Volet m&eacute;nages ordinaires - 2008 (HSM) une enqu&ecirc;te sur les aidants informels (HSA).<br /><br />Cette enqu&ecirc;te HSA permet de caract&eacute;riser les aidants non professionnels (famille, amis, voisins, etc.) de personnes ayant d&eacute;clar&eacute; dans l'enqu&ecirc;te HSM avoir des difficult&eacute;s &agrave; r&eacute;aliser certains actes de la vie quotidienne en raison d'un handicap, d'un probl&egrave;me de sant&eacute; ou de leur &acirc;ge.<br /><br />L'enqu&ecirc;te r&eacute;pond &agrave; un int&eacute;r&ecirc;t soulign&eacute; dans le d&eacute;bat public r&eacute;cent (conf&eacute;rence de la Famille en 2006) permettant d'organiser un droit de r&eacute;pit aux aidants familiaux ; environ 5&nbsp;000 personnes de 16 ans et plus ont &eacute;t&eacute; interrog&eacute;es.<br /><br />Sont abord&eacute;s les caract&eacute;ristiques sociod&eacute;mographiques des aidants de l'entourage : une description de l'activit&eacute; d'aide ; les cons&eacute;quences de l'aide sur la vie familiale et professionnelle des aidants, leur sant&eacute;, leurs loisirs, leurs relations avec les aidants professionnels (de sant&eacute; et du secteur social) compl&eacute;mentarit&eacute;).<br /><br />Par ailleurs, en 2009, est r&eacute;alis&eacute; le volet institution de l'enqu&ecirc;te Handicap-Sant&eacute; (HSI). </p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.3>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.3/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.3/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The data from 39,000 people (including local extensions) was collected by investigators in face-to-face interviews.</p>\n<p>It took place between April and September 2008.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/P> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/territoire/franceHorsMayotte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>- les d&eacute;ficiences et les incapacit&eacute;s (limitations fonctionnelles et restrictions d'activit&eacute;s) ;<br />- la sant&eacute;, la sant&eacute; mentale, la pr&eacute;vention, le recours aux soins, la consommation m&eacute;dicale, l'hospitalisation ;<br />- les diff&eacute;rentes formes d'aides re&ccedil;ues : aides techniques, humaines, prestations, aides &agrave; l'insertion professionnelle, aides &agrave;&nbsp;la scolarit&eacute;&hellip; <br />- le besoin d'aide, sous toutes ses formes ;<br />- la situation familiale, la scolarit&eacute;, l'emploi, les revenus, les loisirs, les vacances, la participation &agrave; la vie associative et les discriminations ressenties&hellip;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.4/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>- Deficiency and disability (functional limitations and activity restrictions)<br />- Health, mental health, prevention, use of care facilities, use of medical facilities and hospitalisation<br />- Different forms of aid received: technical, human, services, help with professional integration, help with schooling, etc.<br />- Need for aid, in all its forms<br />- Family situation, schooling, jobs, income, leisure, holidays, membership of associations and discrimination experienced, etc.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.1.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/uniteEnquetee/I> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.6>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.6>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.6/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.6/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.3.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Les personnes de tout &acirc;ge vivant en m&eacute;nage ordinaire en France, m&eacute;tropole et d&eacute;partements d'outre-mer (DOM).</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.18.3/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>La collecte est r&eacute;alis&eacute;e en face &agrave; face par enqu&ecirc;teur, aupr&egrave;s de 39&nbsp;000 personnes (y compris dans les extensions locales).</p>\n<p>Elle a eu lieu d'avril &agrave; septembre 2008.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.8>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.8>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/modeCollecte/F> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/S.1.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.10>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.10>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.10/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1689/I.18.10/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1689> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/262>
