<http://rdf.insee.fr/graphes/qualite/rapport/1930> {
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The sampling base is the Sirus register (Identification system for the Statistical Units in the Register).<br /><br />The sample is stratified by business sector and by size and, since 2012, by turnover. Depending on the survey year, approximately 12,500 businesses are surveyed.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.18.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/A> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1930> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>To get closer with concepts used in the European survey, since the survey ICT 2011, the size of the questioned units is not any&nbsp;more measured in number of employees, but in number of occupied persons: the non-salaried persons are included in staff. The survey ICT concerns the companies of at least 10 occupied persons, -what includes in particular the units using 9 employees and whose manager is not salaried- the previous survey on those of at least 10 employees. One of the consequences of this modification on the results is an increase of the influence of the smallest companies.</p>\n<p>Since the ICT 2011 survey, the scope has covered businesses with ten employees or more belonging to the following sectors of NACE rev.&nbsp;2: manufacturing industry (section C), production and distribution of electricity, gas, steam and conditioned air (section D), production and distribution of water, sewerage, waste management and cleanup (section E), the building industry (section F), trade, repair of automobiles and motorcycles (section G), transport and warehousing (section H), accommodation and catering (section I), information and communication (section J), real-estate activities (section L), specialist scientific and technical activities, excluding veterinary activities (divisions 69 to 74), administrative service and support activities (section N),&nbsp;repair of computers and communications equipment (group 95.1).</p>\n<p>Since the ICT 2011 survey, the scope doesn't covered financial and insurance societies. The following sectors are excluded:<br />- other monetary intermediations and other distributions of credit (classes 64.19 and 64.92),<br />- insurance and re-insurance (groups 65.1 and 65.2),<br />- auxiliary financial service activities, excluding insurance, pension funds and financial market administration (classes 66.12 and 66.19).</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.3.3/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Sections C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, L, N, divisions 69 &agrave; 74 et groupe 95 de la NAF rev.&nbsp;2.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.3.5>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.3.5>
                    "Legal unit enterprise"@en , "Unités légales"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1930> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.10.2/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Insee Premi&egrave;re, Insee R&eacute;sultats</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1930>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Quality report: Survey on information and communication technologies in business 2020"@en , "Rapport qualité : Enquête sur les technologies de l'information et de la communication dans les entreprises 2020"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/operations/operation/s1486> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.5>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.5>
                    "<p>La p&eacute;riode de r&eacute;f&eacute;rence est 2020 pour la plupart des questions&nbsp;; le dernier exercice comptable (2019) pour le commerce &eacute;lectronique.</p>"@fr , "<p>The reference period is mainly 2020 except for the characteristics referring to the previous accounting year (turnover, websales).</p>"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1930> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1930/S.3.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Pour se rapprocher des concepts utilis&eacute;s dans l'enqu&ecirc;te europ&eacute;enne, depuis l'&eacute;dition 2011 de l'enqu&ecirc;te TIC, la taille des unit&eacute;s interrog&eacute;es n'est plus mesur&eacute;e en nombre de salari&eacute;s, mais en nombre de personnes occup&eacute;es&nbsp;: les personnes non-salari&eacute;es sont incluses dans les effectifs. L'enqu&ecirc;te TIC 2011 porte ainsi sur les soci&eacute;t&eacute;s d'au moins 10 personnes occup&eacute;es, - ce qui comprend&nbsp;notamment les unit&eacute;s employant 9 salari&eacute;s et dont le dirigeant est non salari&eacute; - les enqu&ecirc;tes pr&eacute;c&eacute;dentes sur celles d'au moins&nbsp;10 salari&eacute;s. L'une des cons&eacute;quences de cette modification sur les r&eacute;sultats est une augmentation de l'influence des plus petites soci&eacute;t&eacute;s.</p>\n<p>&Aacute; partir de l'enqu&ecirc;te TIC2011, le champ couvre les entreprises-unit&eacute;s l&eacute;gales appartenant aux secteurs suivants de la NACE r&eacute;v.&nbsp;2&nbsp;: l'industrie manufacturi&egrave;re (section C), la production et la distribution d'&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, de gaz, de vapeur et&nbsp;d'air conditionn&eacute; (section D), la production et la distribution d'eau, l'assainissement, la gestion des d&eacute;chets et la d&eacute;pollution (section E), la construction (section F), le commerce, la r&eacute;paration d'automobiles et de motocycles (section G), les transports et l'entreposage (section H), l'h&eacute;bergement et la restauration (section I), l'information et la communication (section J), les activit&eacute;s immobili&egrave;res (section L), les activit&eacute;s sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;es, scientifiques et techniques hors activit&eacute;s v&eacute;t&eacute;rinaires (divisions 69 &agrave; 74), les activit&eacute;s de services administratifs et de soutien (section N), la r&eacute;paration d'ordinateurs et d'&eacute;quipements de communication (groupe 95.1).</p>\n<p>&Aacute; partir de l'enqu&ecirc;te 2011, les soci&eacute;t&eacute;s financi&egrave;res et d'assurance sont exclues. Les secteurs d'activit&eacute; suivants ne font plus partie du champ de l'enqu&ecirc;te, contrairement aux ann&eacute;es pr&eacute;c&eacute;dentes&nbsp;:<br />- les autres interm&eacute;diations mon&eacute;taires et les autres distributions de cr&eacute;dit (classes 64.19 et 64.92 de la NAF r&eacute;v. 2)&nbsp;;<br />- l'assurance et la r&eacute;assurance (groupes 65.1 et 65.2)&nbsp;;<br />- l'administration de march&eacute;s financiers et les autres activit&eacute;s auxiliaires de services financiers, hors assurance et caisses de retraite (classes 66.11 et 66.19).</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
