    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1956/S.18.5/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The weighting adjustement is done in two steps. <br />The weights are first adjusted by estimating the response probabilities using a logistic regression (with auxiliary variables&nbsp;: type of address, previous non-response status, type of housing, geographical location).<br />Then, a calibration is done on individual margins (disaggregated by gender and age group, diploma, place of birth) and on housing external margins (number of main residences).</p>"@en ;
