                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.10.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.2/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.2/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.1.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.1.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/organisations/insee/DG75-E001> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.7/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.7/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.6>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.6>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.6/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.6/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.3/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Sections C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, L, N, divisions 69 &agrave; 74 et groupe 95 de la NAF rev. 2.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.19/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The EC survey on the \"use of ICT and electronic commerce\" in business is a set of surveys conducted by the national institutes of statistics of the member countries of the European Union.<br /><br />It complies with regulation n&deg;808/2004 adopted on April 21, 2004&nbsp;as part of the implementation of the 2005 eEurope action plan devoted to information and communication technologies: this regulation was amended by European regulation n&deg; 1006/2009 of September 16, 2009. Accordingly, the surveys on ICT and electronic commerce in business conducted by the countries of the European Union follow a common methodology and the same model of questionnaire.<br /><br />Each year, one or more topics, determined by the annual European regulation for&nbsp;the implementation of the framework regulation, are developed in particular.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.7/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>January to April</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.12.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.12.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.12.1/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.12.1/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.5>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.5>
                    "<p>La p&eacute;riode de r&eacute;f&eacute;rence est 2014 pour la plupart des questions&nbsp;; le dernier exercice comptable (2013) pour le commerce &eacute;lectronique.</p>"@fr , "<p>The reference period is mainly 2014 except for the characteristics referring to the previous accounting year (turnover, websales).</p>"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.11>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.11>
                    "<p>16 000</p>"@fr , "<p>16,000</p>"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.4/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The topics covered are: the development of new technologies and the intensity of their use in business; the types of use of ICT&nbsp;(electronic commerce, sharing and exchanging of information and, more generally, relations with the world outside the business); the obstacles and impacts of this dissemination.<br /><br />Each year, some topics, determined by the annual European regulation for the implementation of the framework regulation, are developed in particular. In 2014: ICT specialists and skills, Electronic invoicing, Use of cloud computing services, Sharing Supply Chain Management information electronically, Automatic sharing of information within the enterprise, Use of RFID technologies, Use of EDI-type messages suitable for automated processing. Besides, e-Sales are investigated in an extra module.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.2/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Insee Premi&egrave;re, Insee R&eacute;sultats</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The following categories of the NACE Rev. 2 : sections C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, L, N, divisions 69 to 74, group 95.1.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.6.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.6.4>
                    "2014A016EC"@fr , "2014A016EC"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.6>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.10.6>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.6/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The sampling base is the Sirus register (Identification system for the Statistical Units in the Register).<br /><br />The sample is stratified by business sector and by size and, since 2012, by turnover. Depending on the survey year, approximately 12,500 businesses are surveyed.<br /><br />For ICT 2014, an extra sample (3,500 businesses) was added in order to conduct a module dedicated to e-Sales.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.10>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.10>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.10/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.18.10/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Quality report: Survey on information and communication technologies in business 2014"@en , "Rapport qualité : Enquête sur les technologies de l'information et de la communication dans les entreprises 2014"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/operations/operation/s1064> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>To get closer with concepts used in the European survey, since the survey ICT 2011, the size of the questioned units is not any&nbsp;more measured in number of employees, but in number of occupied persons: the non-salaried persons are included in staff. The survey ICT concerns the companies of at least 10 occupied persons, - what includes in particular the units using 9 employees and whose manager is not salaried - the previous survey on those of at least 10 employees. One of the consequences of this modification on the results is an increase of the influence of the smallest companies.<br /><br />Since the ICT 2011 survey, the scope has covered businesses with ten employees or more belonging to the following sectors of NACE rev. 2: manufacturing industry (section C), production and distribution of electricity, gas, steam and conditioned air (section D), production and distribution of water, sewerage, waste management and cleanup (section E), the building industry (section F), trade, repair of automobiles and motorcycles (section G), transport and warehousing (section H), accommodation and catering (section I), information and communication (section J), real-estate activities (section L), specialist scientific and technical activities, excluding veterinary activities (divisions 69 to 74), administrative service and support activities (section N),&nbsp;repair of computers and communications equipment (group 95.1).<br /><br />Since the ICT 2011 survey, the scope doesn't covered financial and insurance societies. The following sectors are excluded :<br />- other monetary intermediations and other distributions of credit (classes 64.19 and 64.92),<br />- insurance and re-insurance (groups 65.1 and 65.2),<br />- auxiliary financial service activities, excluding insurance, pension funds and financial market administration (classes 66.12 and 66.19).</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/145>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Qualité de l'enquête relative à l'exercice 2014"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2015-07-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/BIL_EN_TIC_2014_internet.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.6/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Pour se rapprocher des concepts utilis&eacute;s dans l'enqu&ecirc;te europ&eacute;enne, depuis l'&eacute;dition 2011 de l'enqu&ecirc;te TIC, la taille des unit&eacute;s interrog&eacute;es n'est plus mesur&eacute;e en nombre de salari&eacute;s, mais en nombre de personnes occup&eacute;es : les personnes non-salari&eacute;es sont incluses dans les effectifs. L'enqu&ecirc;te TIC 2011 porte ainsi sur les soci&eacute;t&eacute;s d'au moins 10 personnes occup&eacute;es, - ce qui comprend&nbsp;notamment les unit&eacute;s employant 9 salari&eacute;s et dont le dirigeant est non salari&eacute; - les enqu&ecirc;tes pr&eacute;c&eacute;dentes sur celles d'au moins&nbsp;10 salari&eacute;s. L'une des cons&eacute;quences de cette modification sur les r&eacute;sultats est une augmentation de l'influence des plus petites soci&eacute;t&eacute;s.<br /><br />A partir de l'enqu&ecirc;te TIC2011, le champ couvre les entreprises-unit&eacute;s l&eacute;gales appartenant aux secteurs suivants de la NACE&nbsp; r&eacute;v. 2 : l'industrie manufacturi&egrave;re (section C), la production et la distribution d'&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, de gaz, de vapeur et&nbsp;d'air conditionn&eacute; (section D), la production et la distribution d'eau, l'assainissement, la gestion des d&eacute;chets et la d&eacute;pollution (section E), la construction (section F), le commerce, la r&eacute;paration d'automobiles et de motocycles (section G), les transports et l'entreposage (section H), l'h&eacute;bergement et la restauration (section I), l'information et la communication (section J), les activit&eacute;s immobili&egrave;res (section L), les activit&eacute;s sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;es, scientifiques et techniques hors activit&eacute;s v&eacute;t&eacute;rinaires (divisions 69 &agrave; 74), les activit&eacute;s de services administratifs et de soutien (section N), la r&eacute;paration d'ordinateurs et d'&eacute;quipements de communication (groupe 95.1). <br /><br />A partir de l'enqu&ecirc;te 2011, les soci&eacute;t&eacute;s financi&egrave;res et d'assurance sont exclues. Les secteurs d'activit&eacute; suivants ne font plus partie du champ de l'enqu&ecirc;te, contrairement aux ann&eacute;es pr&eacute;c&eacute;dentes :<br />- les autres interm&eacute;diations mon&eacute;taires et les autres distributions de cr&eacute;dit (classes 64.19 et 64.92 de la NAF r&eacute;v. 2) ;<br />- l'assurance et la r&eacute;assurance (groupes 65.1 et 65.2) ;<br />- l'administration de march&eacute;s financiers et les autres activit&eacute;s auxiliaires de services financiers, hors assurance et caisses de retraite (classes 66.11 et 66.19).</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.18.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The collection, conducted by internet since 2012 (or by paper questionnaire on request), is launched in the first quarter of the year in question.<br />The survey covers the whole of France (geography at the time of collection).</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/A> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.4>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.4/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.4/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Les th&egrave;mes abord&eacute;s sont : le d&eacute;veloppement des nouvelles technologies et l'intensit&eacute; de leur utilisation au sein de l'entreprise ; les types d'utilisation des TIC (commerce &eacute;lectronique, partage et &eacute;change d'information, plus g&eacute;n&eacute;ralement les relations avec le monde externe &agrave; l'entreprise) ; les obstacles et l'impact de cette diffusion.<br /><br />Chaque ann&eacute;e, certains th&egrave;mes, d&eacute;termin&eacute;s par le r&egrave;glement europ&eacute;en annuel d'application du r&egrave;glement cadre, font l'objet d'un d&eacute;veloppement particulier. En 2014, les th&egrave;mes abord&eacute;s sont les sp&eacute;cialistes en TIC et comp&eacute;tences, la facturation inter-entreprises, le cloud-computing, le partage &eacute;lectronique d&rsquo;information sur le SCM, le partage automatique d&rsquo;information au sein de l&rsquo;entreprise, l&rsquo;utilisation des technologies RFID, l&rsquo;utilisation de messages de type EDI permettant un traitement automatique. Les ventes &eacute;lectroniques font l&rsquo;objet d&rsquo;un module suppl&eacute;mentaire.</p>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/I.6.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.6.3>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/statutEnquete/T> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1732> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1732/S.10.2/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Insee Premi&egrave;re, Insee R&eacute;sultats</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
}

<http://rdf.insee.fr/graphes/qualite/rapport/1720> {
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/I.18.10>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.10>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/I.18.10/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/I.18.10/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1720> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/S.7.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>Law n&deg; 51-711 of 7 June 1951 on obligations, co-ordination and confidentiality in respect of statistics. Available from https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/affichTexte.do?cidTexte=JORFTEXT000000888573.</p>\n<p>Article 6 concerns statistical confidentiality: Subject to the provisions of Articles 40, 56, 76, 97 and 99 of the Code of Criminal Procedure and those of Article L. 213-3 of the French Heritage Code, the individual information contained in the questionnaires endorsed as provided for in Article 2 of this Law and relating to private and family life and, in general, to private acts and conduct can not, unless decided by the Archives Administration, after examining the opinion of the Statistical Confidentiality Committee and relating to a request made for the purposes of public statistics or scientific or historical research, be the subject of any communication by the depositary service before the expiry of a period of seventy-five years following the date of completion of the survey or a period of twenty-five years from the death of the person concerned, whichever is the shorter.<br />A Statistical Confidentiality Committee is set up. This committee is called upon to rule on any question relating to the confidentiality of statistics. It expresses its opinion on requests for the communication of individual data collected pursuant to this law. The committee is chaired by a State Councillor, appointed by the Vice-President of the Council of State. It includes in particular representatives of the French National Assembly and Senate. The composition and operating methods of the committee are set by decree of the Council of State. Recipients of the data communications resulting from Ministerial decisions made after consulting the Statistical Confidentiality Committee agree to not communicate these data to anyone. Any violation of the provisions of this paragraph is punishable by the penalties provided for in Article 226-13 of the Penal Code.</p>\n<p>Act no. 78-17 of 6 January 1978(amended), relating to information technology, files and civil freedoms.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/S.10.7/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/937> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/S.10.2/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "<p>The data are published in the INSEE Results section and available at insee.fr.</p>"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1720/S.12.1/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
